From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t41: map the raw-inject buffer with ioremap

The mainline kernel removed ioremap_nocache(), so the raw-inject path
leaves the module with an undefined symbol at modpost.  Map the buffer
with ioremap(), which is uncached on this target.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t41/tx_isp_t41_rawinject.c
+++ b/driver/t41/tx_isp_t41_rawinject.c
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
 		pr_err("t41_rawinject: isp_malloc_buffer(%u) failed (ispmem/rmem?)\n", bytes);
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
-	rj_virt = ioremap_nocache(rj_paddr, bytes);
+	rj_virt = ioremap(rj_paddr, bytes);
 	if (!rj_virt) {
 		isp_free_buffer(rj_paddr);
 		rj_paddr = 0;
